  :doc/body "# Traversal bounds, measured 2026-09-10

ADR-2609108000 listed IPLD traversal bounds as **unmeasured**, and unmeasured
is not clean. This is the measurement. It EXERCISES each seam rather than
grepping for the word limit — a seam that names a limit and defaults it to
unlimited reads exactly like one that enforces it, and grep cannot tell them
apart.

Harness `scripts/measure-traversal-bounds.cljs`, 16 assertions, exit 0.
Run it from the superproject root, or pass `--root <checkout>`; section F
reads the west-managed `orgs/` tree and **fails closed** rather than
reporting a pass when it cannot.

## Bounded, fail closed, no default

| seam | required | on missing |
|---|---|---|
| `ipld.graph/selection-cursor` | `:max-blocks` `:max-bytes` `:max-depth` `:max-matches` | throws `:ipld/invalid-limit` **before reading a block** |
| `prolly-tree.diff/sync-blocks*` | `:max-blocks` `:max-bytes` `:max-reads` | throws `:prolly-tree/invalid-limit`, and `0` is not a limit |

Both refuse a partial set, not merely an empty one — three of the four is
still a refusal. There is no permissive default to fall back on. Measured.

## Unbounded, on the path the query plane uses

`prolly-tree.core/scan-prefix` has two arities and they differ in exactly
this:

    (scan-prefix get-fn root prefix)        ; limit = nil = UNLIMITED
    (scan-prefix get-fn root prefix limit)  ; bounded

On a 400-entry tree the 3-arity returns 400; the 4-arity with 5 returns 5;
`0` returns empty without walking. `scan-range` takes no limit parameter at
all — its arity is `[get-fn root-cid lo hi]`, and a nil bound is unbounded.

**Both call sites the deployed read path uses take the 3-arity:**

- `arrangement/core.cljc` — snapshot hydrate, empty prefix, no limit, and it
  decrypts every leaf it reads.
- `arrangement/source.cljc` — pattern read, key-range pruned by
  `key-prefix`, still no limit.

Section F pins those two call sites by exact anchor and **fails if an anchor
is not found exactly once**, so a moved call site reads as a finding rather
than as a silent pass.

## What this composes with

It is the same shape as the ayatori finding recorded in
`orgs/kotoba-lang/ayatori` `bench/inference-channel-01.edn`: cost follows the
database rather than the answer, everywhere on this path, and the ceiling
that notices is the thing that reports the size. **The bound is not missing
from the codebase. It is missing from the two doors the query plane walks
through.**

## Not concluded here

- Whether the hydrate SHOULD be bounded. A snapshot hydrate that must read
  the whole snapshot is bounded only by refusing to serve large graphs, and
  `materialize` already chose to do exactly that with a ceiling. Which of the
  two behaviours belongs on which path is a decision.
- Decompression ratio, listed alongside the other bounds in ADR-2609108000,
  is not applicable on the pack path: that path measured a compression ratio
  of 1.003 on ciphertext and decided not to compress. Nothing to bomb.
- Fanout is bounded implicitly by `:max-blocks` on the seams that have it and
  not at all on the two that do not. It is not separately measured.

## Both directions

- Break the countdown so counts change (`(take (inc @left) ms)`): exit 1, and
  the failures are `4-arity with a limit stops` and `boundary: limit == n-1`.
  **The `limit == n` probe does not move** — only the pair separates them,
  which is why the pair is there.
- A first attempt broke the descent guard instead (`(pos? @left)` to
  `(>= @left 0)`) and the harness stayed green. That break changes how many
  blocks are read and not how many entries come back, so it was the wrong
  break, not a blind spot. Recorded because the mistake is the cheap one to
  make.
- Move an anchor in section F: exit 1, `anchor found 0 times`.
- Unmodified: exit 0, `SCANNED 16`."}]
